#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md:6
msgid "Soundness Proof (Part 2)"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md:8
msgid ""
"A sound function is one that can't trigger UB if its safety preconditions "
"are satisfied."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md:11
msgid "Corollary: All functions implemented in pure safe Rust are sound."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md:13
msgid "Proof:"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md:15
msgid "Safe Rust code has no safety preconditions."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md:17
msgid ""
"Therefore, callers of functions implemented in pure safe Rust always "
"trivially satisfy the empty set of preconditions."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md:20
msgid "Safe Rust code can't trigger UB."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md:22
msgid "QED."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md:26
msgid "Read the corollary."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md:28
msgid "Explain the proof."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/soundness-proof/corollary.md:30
msgid ""
"Translate into informal terms: all safe Rust code is nice. It does not have "
"safety preconditions that the programmer has to think of, always plays by "
"the rules, and never triggers UB."
msgstr ""
